{
  "_STATUS": "DRAFT — AUTHORED, NOT CLINICALLY APPROVED. NOT FOR PATIENT USE.",
  "_whatThisIs": [
    "Patient-reported intake questions for this AYUSH system: things the patient",
    "observes about themselves and can answer without training. Every answer is",
    "stored PATIENT-REPORTED and no part of this produces a diagnosis, a",
    "classification or a remedy.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT: the constitutional and diagnostic instruments of",
    "each system — Prakriti and Vikriti in Ayurveda, Mizaj in Unani, Thegu/Nyes-pa",
    "in Sowa-Rigpa, and their equivalents. Those are classification tools whose",
    "output a clinician acts on, and a plausible-looking version of one is worse",
    "than none: it reads correct to a reviewer skimming it and is wrong in ways",
    "only a practitioner of that system can see. They remain AWAITING_AUTHORSHIP."
  ],
  "_beforeThisCanBePublished": [
    "A registered practitioner OF THIS SYSTEM reviews every question here.",
    "A second practitioner approves it — nobody approves their own work.",
    "A translation reviewer approves each language.",
    "A safety reviewer checks the failure modes.",
    "Published through the governance console, which enforces all four."
  ],
